<title>DENMARK: FORECAST - Morgan Stanley ups Danish 96 c/a surplus.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Morgan Stanley ups Danish 96 c/a surplus.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>In its latest survey U.S. investment bank Morgan Stanley on Monday upped its expectations for Denmark's 1996 current account surplus to 10.0 billion crowns from 6.3 billion crowns in its June forecast.</p>
<p>At the same time it left unchanged its forecast for inflation at 2.1 percent and its expectations for gross domestic product) growth at 1.9 percent.</p>
<p>The latest Danish Economy Ministry forecast in August foresaw 1.8 percent GDP growth, 2.0 percent inflation, 9.0 percent unemployment and a current account surplus of 10.0 billion crowns for this year.</p>
<p>The following estimates were made by 10 leading local and international organisations.</p>
<p>		(pct)  GDP    inflation unemployment  c/a (bln crns)</p>
<p>Morgan St (10/96)  1.9    2.1	  9.0	    10.0</p>
<p>Danske Bank (9/96) 1.2    2.1	  9.0	     7.4</p>
<p>PaineWebber (9/96) 1.7    2.1	  8.5	     8.1</p>
<p>Citibank (9/96)    1.1    2.2	  7.7	     7.5</p>
<p>NatWest  (9/96)    1.5    2.1	  9.0	     6.9</p>
<p>Spar Nord (9/96)   1.5    2.1	  9.0	    10.0</p>
<p>AE Council (9/96)  2.0    2.1	  8.9	    12.0</p>
<p>Lehman Bros (8/96) 1.7    2.1	  8.9	     --</p>
<p>M.Grenfell (8/96)  1.5    2.1	  9.0	    12.0</p>
<p>Indosuez (8/96)    2.2    2.2	  8.9	    19.0</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
